# The SKIP lines runtime/test/build.sh prints ON CI (ci.yml's
# `drivers' job, ubuntu-24.04 with the packages that job installs),
# held as text: M9_SKIPS=runtime/test/build.skips makes any other set
# a failure.  A battery that skips where it is meant to run is a red
# diff here instead of a green exit; a line that disappears because
# the job gained a library is a red diff too, and the fix is to delete
# the line -- which is the record that the battery now runs.
#
# `#' lines and blank lines are not compared.  A line starting `? ' is
# OPTIONAL: it may appear or not (the network decides) and is left out
# of the comparison on both sides.  Order does not matter.
#
# This is CI's list and no other machine's: the release machine has
# pyarrow, xarray and cfchecks and skips four lines, not eight.

# data that is not in the repository and is not fetched
SKIP: csv_driver (the FLUXNET battery: no /mnt/d/data/ICOSETC_SE-Htm_FLUXNET_HH_L2.csv; set $M9CSV)
SKIP: no real GRIB at /mnt/d/data/grib/EA25120100 (set $M9GRIB)
SKIP live Carbon Portal checks (set M9HTTP_LIVE=1)

# Python packages the job does not install: the M9-reads-theirs half
# of each is gated by checked-in goldens, the theirs-reads-M9 half is
# what these lines say did not run
SKIP: cfchecks not installed
SKIP: pyarrow not installed
SKIP: pyarrow not installed (the cross-read half)
SKIP: xarray half (no xarray)
SKIP: .zmetadata byte-identity needs zarr 3 (have 2.17.0)

# the runner's route to the outside
? SKIP: no route to zarr.icos-cp.eu; TLS network checks not run
